        "original_id": "7861b2f6-8c32-5176-a6c7-17e1a64790d4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Denmark Hill, Camberwell, London Borough of Southwark, London, Palace of Westminster, Wanganui, New Zealand\n- Landmarks: Big Ben, Great Bell, clock tower, Big Ben clockface\n- People: Frank William Gilligan\n- Organizations: Oxford University, Essex county side\n- Topics: cricket\n\nFacts:\n- Denmark Hill is an area and road in Camberwell in the London Borough of Southwark.\n- On a clear day, Denmark Hill offers a view from which one can read the time on the Big Ben clockface.\n- Big Ben is the nickname for the Great Bell of the clock at the north end of the Palace of Westminster in London.\n- Big Ben usually also refers to the clock and the clock tower at the Palace of Westminster.\n- Frank William Gilligan was born on 20 September 1893 in Denmark Hill, London.\n- Frank William Gilligan was an English cricketer who played for Oxford University and was an integral part of the Essex county side for ten years.\n- Frank William Gilligan died on 4 May 1960 in Wanganui, New Zealand.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
