        "text": "Page: Denmark Hill. Sentence: Denmark Hill is an area and road in Camberwell, in the London Borough of Southwark.\nPage: Denmark Hill. Sentence: On a clear day one can read the time on the Big Ben clockface.\nPage: Big Ben. Sentence: Big Ben is the nickname for the Great Bell of the clock at the north end of the Palace of Westminster in London and is usually extended to refer to both the clock and the clock tower as well.\nPage: Frank Gilligan. Sentence: Frank William Gilligan OBE (20 September 1893 in Denmark Hill, London – 4 May 1960 in Wanganui, New Zealand) was an English cricketer who played for Oxford University and was an integral part of the Essex county side for ten years.",
